{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>אף</b> — Rabbi Marinus said: that it is like \"אף וכני בתי חומר\" [indeed, like houses of clay]; they did no iniquity, to transgress the word of HaShem in negative commandments, but walked in the ways of HaShem, which are positive commandments. And it is possible that it is according to its plain meaning: also, one who did no iniquity — it will be accounted to him that he walked in the ways of HaShem."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:08.416486160Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}